window.products.push({"id":482345,"name":"DC50 Upright Vacuum with Bonus Accessories","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31TZG1eX13L._AC_.jpg","description":"DC50 is Dyson’s lightest upright vacuum. It weighs just 11.6 lbs. and has the performance of a full-size upright. The technology inside has not simply been concentrated – every angle and dimension re-engineered for improved performance. Dyson DC50 has advanced cleaner head technology. It includes a self-adjusting base plate for optimal contact on every floor type, a brush bar with anti-static carbon fiber bristles to remove fine dust from hard floors and stiff nylon bristles to remove ground-in dirt from carpets. Like all Dyson vacuums, DC50 has no bag, so there’s no loss of suction. Instead, patented cyclone technology spins dust and dirt from the air. With 2 Tier Radial cyclones, DC50 Animal has 19 cyclones that work in parallel across two tiers to increase airflow and capture more microscopic dust from the home. Unlike ordinary upright vacuum cleaners, DC50 rides on a ball. It turns on the spot, steering easily around furniture and into difficult places. DC50 has Dyson’s latest Ball technology. Even more of the machine’s key components are located inside the ball itself. This reduces clutter on the outside of the machine, streamlining its profile. DC50 is certified by the Asthma and Allergy Foundation of America and includes AAFA certified tools: carbon fiber soft dusting brush, flexi-crevice reach under tool and mattress. Advanced cleaner head technology – self-adjusting cleaner head for optimal contact on every floor type; carbon fiber bristles remove fine dust from hard floors 2 tier radial cyclones – Dyson cyclones capture more microscopic dust than any other Latest Ball technology – turns on a dime Light and durable – weighs just 11.6 lbs. Includes AAFA certified allergy tools: carbon fiber soft dusting brush, flexi-crevice reach under tool and mattress tool Instant release wand for cleaning awkward areas Quick and hygienic bin emptying No extra costs – no replacement bags or filters to buy 5-year warranty, parts and labor","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31TZG1eX13L._AC_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Dyson","source_asin":"B00SQK87UG","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-482345","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00SQK87UG","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B00SQK87UG","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
window.products.push({"id":482346,"name":"Bodum Shin Bistro 12-Ounce French Press, Black, One Size","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":29.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71mTU+xzOKS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Product Description The Bodum Shin Bistro French press coffee maker is accepted worldwide as one of the best methods for brewing coffee. Coffee is measured in 4 oz. cups, so our 3 cup press will brew 12 oz; the perfect size for brewing single servings of your favorite coffee. The patented safety lid prevents the squirting of liquids. It features a black stay-cool, non-slip rubber handle. The body is made of high-tech, ultra-light heat-resistant borosilicate glass and is a great hit for those who want to combat life's daily stresses with a perfect cup of coffee at anytime. All parts are dishwasher safe. The Shin Bistro is also available in 4, 8 and 12 cup models. Amazon.com A satisfying alternative to cranking up the automatic drip coffeemaker for a single cup, the Bodum Shin Bistro small coffee press makes delicious coffee with little effort. A blend of heat-resistant borosilicate glass and a stainless-steel rod filter system, the piece turns out coffee in four minutes or less. Simply add water and grounds, wait a bit, and plunge the filter. A fine screen keeps grounds at the bottom while letting natural oils through for optimum flavor. This version of the time-tested design includes a non-slip handle, a stay-cool knob, and a trim see-through beaker for best display of coffee colors. It holds 12 ounces and is safe in the dishwasher. Larger versions are also available. --Emily Bedard From the Manufacturer Awards and Accolades In 2004 the Bodum Chambord coffee press received the American Culinary Institute's award for best French press coffeemaker. The American Culinary Institute judges food preparation products such as mixers, waffle makers, and electric teakettles. These products are judged on criteria important to consumers such as ease-of-use, safety, and the quality of the food produced. The institute also judges food preparation products used in restaurants and hotels, including institutional mixers, large-volume coffee machines, and food slicers. Instructions for Use 1. Place pot on a dry, flat, nonslip surface. Hold handle firmly, then pull the plunger straight up and out of the pot. 2. For each 1.25-deciliter/4-ounce cup, put 1 rounded tablespoon or 1 Bodum scoop of coarse-ground coffee into the pot. Caution: Use only coarse-ground coffee. Fine grind can clog the filter and create high pressure. Place coffee maker on a heatproof, nonslip surface. 3. Pour hot (not boiling) water into the pot. Leave a minimum of 2.5 centimeters/1 inch of space at the top. Stir the brew with a plastic spoon. Caution: Metal spoons can scratch or chip the glass beaker and cause breakage. 4. Place the plunger unit on top of the pot. Turn lid to close off the pour spout opening. (Does not apply to the Brazil models.) Do not press down. Let the coffee brew for at least 4 minutes. 5. Hold the pot handle firmly, with the spout turned away from you, then using just the weight of your hand, apply slight pressure on top of the knob to lower the plunger straight down into the pot. Lowering the plunger slowly with minimal pressure produces best results. If the filter clogs or it becomes difficult to push down the plunger you should remove the plunger from the pot, stir the brew, and then slowly plunge again. WARNING: Using excessive force can cause scalding liquid to shoot out of the pot. 6. Turn the lid to open the pour spout and then pour coffee. 7. Unscrew the filter assembly and clean the plunger unit after each use. All parts are dishwasher-safe. Safety Instructions Not for stovetop use. Not for stovetop use. Check glass beaker for scratches, cracks, or chips. Do not use a pot that is scratched, chipped, or cracked. Install a replacement beaker before using the pot again. Check glass beaker for scratches, cracks, or chips. Do not use a pot that is scratched, chipped, or cracked. Install a replacement beaker before using the pot again. Keep children away while using. Hot water is a hazard to small children! Keep children away while using. Hot water is a hazard to small children! Do not allow children to use this coffeemaker. Scald Hazard Excessive plunging force can cause scalding hot liquid to shoot out of pot. Do not plunge with force. Turn lid to close spout. Use only coarse-ground coffee. Company History In 1944 Peter Bodum, the father of today's owner, Joergen Bodum, started Bodum in Copenhagen. Times were difficult at the end of World War II; there was hardly any trade and people were out of work. Peter Bodum managed to wholesale a very small variety of housewares products by Danish manufacturers.  After the war Peter Bodum got an import license for kitchen and tabletop products; he traveled all over Europe and ended up importing kitchen and housewares to Denmark. As in the rest of Europe in those days, a lack of products in Denmark meant a market existed for almost anything to be sold. He specialized in glassware from Eastern Europe.  In the '50s Peter Bodum started developing his own products. He collaborated with the D","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71mTU+xzOKS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Bodum","source_asin":"B004UMINDA","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-482346","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B004UMINDA","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B004UMINDA","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
